+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1
+
+**Base commit:** HEAD (initial state, no prior commits with role-advanced work).
+
+**Specs authored:** 9 feature files, 35 scenarios covering the TodoMVC spec at `assets/app-spec.md`.
+
+**Production deliverables needed:**
+- `index.html` at project root (adapted from `assets/app-template.index.html`)
+- `js/app.js` (vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors)
+- `css/app.css` (minimal overrides, base.css and index.css from todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css via node_modules)
+
+**Key design decisions:**
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs` (per spec's `todos-[framework]` convention)
+- Routing via `hashchange` event on `window`, filtering at model level
+- No external dependencies beyond todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css (devDependencies already installed: @cucumber/cucumber, happy-dom)
+- The test harness (`features/support/world.js`) loads `index.html` and `js/app.js`, executes via happy-dom `window.eval`, and fires DOMContentLoaded/load events
diff --git a/specs/clear-completed.feature b/specs/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..445e8da
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos with one click
+  So that I can clean up finished work
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed todos
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the app has a completed todo "Clean house"
+    When the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then the todo "Clean house" does not exist
+    And a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the clear completed button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed unchecks toggle all
+    Given the app has completed todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    Then the toggle all checkbox is checked
+    When the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then the toggle all checkbox is unchecked
+    And the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
diff --git a/specs/counter.feature b/specs/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..92eba00
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos remain
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero when no todos exist
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Counter reflects active todos only
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the app has a completed todo "Clean house"
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses correct pluralization
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+    When the user types "Clean house" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo count shows "2 items left"
diff --git a/specs/edit-todo.feature b/specs/edit-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dd4de99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/edit-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Edit todo title
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update what I need to do
+
+  Scenario: Activating edit mode on double-click
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo has class "editing"
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+    And the edit input has focus
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo with title "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input and blurs
+    Then a todo with title "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Discarding an edit on Escape
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Destroying a todo with an empty edit
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" does not exist
+    And the main section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from edited titles
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the "Buy groceries" todo label
+    And the user types "  Buy milk  " in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo with title "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
diff --git a/specs/new-todo.feature b/specs/new-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..89fedb0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: New todo creation
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos by typing in the input field
+  So that I can track things I need to do
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo with valid text
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+    And the new todo input is empty
+    And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from new todo titles
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Preventing empty todos from being created
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Focusing the input on page load
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the new todo input has focus
+
+  Scenario: Creating multiple todos
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "First todo" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Second todo" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 2 todos
+    And the todo count shows "2 items left"
diff --git a/specs/persistence.feature b/specs/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..02c2b5a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: LocalStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then a todo with title "Buy groceries" appears in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across reload
+    Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: localStorage key format
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage contains a key matching "todos-*"
diff --git a/specs/routing.feature b/specs/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f3cf49f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Route-based filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todo list by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I can focus on the relevant subset
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the app has a todo "Active task" and a completed todo "Done task"
+    And the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is visible
+    And the todo "Done task" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Active route hides completed todos
+    Given the app has a todo "Active task" and a completed todo "Done task"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is visible
+    And the todo "Done task" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Completed route hides active todos
+    Given the app has a todo "Active task" and a completed todo "Done task"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Active task" is not visible
+    And the todo "Done task" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Selected filter link reflects current route
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the "All" filter link is selected
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo hides it in active filter
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
diff --git a/specs/toggle-all.feature b/specs/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..64ff29e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: Mark all as complete
+  As a user
+  I want to toggle all todos to complete or active with one checkbox
+  So that I can efficiently manage bulk state changes
+
+  Scenario: Marking all todos as complete
+    Given the app has todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then all todos have class "completed"
+    And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+    And the toggle all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking all todos
+    Given the app has completed todos "Buy groceries" and "Clean house"
+    When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+    Then no todos have class "completed"
+    And the todo count shows "2 items left"
+    And the toggle all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all reflects individual todo state
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the app has a completed todo "Clean house"
+    Then the toggle all checkbox is unchecked
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the toggle all checkbox is checked
diff --git a/specs/toggle-todo.feature b/specs/toggle-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f9fea3f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/toggle-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active by clicking their checkbox
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Scenario: Marking a todo as complete
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo has class "completed"
+    And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Unmarking a completed todo
+    Given the app has a completed todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user toggles the "Buy groceries" todo checkbox
+    Then the "Buy groceries" todo does not have class "completed"
+    And the todo count shows "1 item left"
diff --git a/specs/visibility.feature b/specs/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..14fe716
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Feature: Section visibility
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show only relevant sections
+  So that the interface stays clean
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer hidden when no todos
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer shown when todos exist
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: Removing the last todo hides sections
+    Given the app has a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter on the "Buy groceries" todo
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
